   "plain": "RJ students cross the San Ysidro line twice in a week with a U.S. passport. Most Tijuana residents need a U.S. visitor visa (B1/B2, or a Border Crossing Card) to go north for a day. They must apply, pay a non-refundable fee, interview at a consulate, and show ties to Mexico (job, house, bank account) to be approved. The same bridge has two prices.",
